  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"terminal#19269\"], \"answer\": \"This matches terminal#19269: launching a .bat/.cmd file opens a transparent, frozen Terminal window (the 'defterm window with no tabs' problem) alongside the real console window. The Terminal team ([user], [user]) acknowledged it and asked for Feedback Hub diagnostics. To help, go to Feedback Hub > Apps > Windows Terminal > Advanced Diagnostics, start recording, reproduce the freeze, and upload the report. Feedback Hub also avoids posting your memory dump publicly. Don't attach the dump to GitHub. Because it is a single WindowsTerminal.exe process, killing it in Task Manager frees the stuck windows, and a reboot often clears it temporarily. Starting Terminal at login did not help the original reporter. The archive has no confirmed fix, so this ticket is still open on that point.\"}",
